Z||000000||jdbaker||09-04-2001||09:01 PM||||Dear List:<P>I looking to replace the stock wheels on my 1987 Mera.  The wheel I've selected is avaiable in either 16x7.5 w/35mm offset or 16x7.5 w/40mm offset.  I took a look at the forum archives and it seems that a 16x7 should have a 35mm offset, but with the extra .5 inch, should I go with the larger 40mm offset?  The car has not been lowered.<P>Also, what's the largest tire size I could go with on the correct wheel, without worry of rubbing or extending beyond the fender lip?<P>Thanks!<P>J.D.||||reg||5
Z||000001||rogergarrison||09-05-2001||06:55 AM||||I have 16X8 on my kit (same as Mera) i have 225/60 and 205/60. front and rear offset is different 4 1/2" and 5 1/2" rear backspacing. What it amounts too is that rears need to come out 2" farther than stock to come out to match the Ferrari body. My rears just barely miss the struts inside, front just miss the lower A-arms. Mines not lowered either.<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=11878523&p=52990885"> ||||reg||1
